Subject: [PATCH] ath11k/NSS: enable the pinned statistics layout on both sides

The pinned recipe specifies NSS_FIRMWARE_VERSION_12_5 via EXTRA_CFLAGS,
but Linux 6.18 no longer adopts that legacy variable. Actual Kbuild probes
show both original sides use a 196-byte peer; changing ath11k alone would
introduce a mismatch. Put the recipe's intended define in NSS ccflags-y
as well, and match it in the NSS-enabled ath11k consumer. Both become
212 bytes. This paired candidate still requires firmware wire validation;
it is not evidence that the installed driver pair was already mismatched.
Apply from a root containing backports/ and nss-drv/, after pinned patches.

--- a/backports/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/Makefile
+++ b/backports/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/Makefile
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause-Clear
+ccflags-$(CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_SUPPORT) += -DNSS_FIRMWARE_VERSION_12_5
 obj-$(CPTCFG_ATH11K) += ath11k.o
 ath11k-y += core.o \
--- a/nss-drv/Makefile
+++ b/nss-drv/Makefile
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 obj-m += qca-nss-drv.o
 
 ccflags-y += $(NSS_DRV_EXTRA_INCLUDES)
+ccflags-y += -DNSS_FIRMWARE_VERSION_12_5
 
 #
 # Regular NSS path
